# UI quality bar

A UI change is not done until it holds up in all four combinations:
**390px and 1360px wide × light and dark theme**.

## Must pass

- No horizontal page scroll at 390px (`document.documentElement.scrollWidth <= innerWidth`).
- No text clipped, overlapping, or running off-screen. Long names and long translations wrap or
  truncate with an ellipsis and a tooltip/title.
- Contrast: body text ≥ 4.5:1, large text and icons ≥ 3:1, in both themes. Use theme tokens, not
  hard-coded colours that only work in one theme.
- Touch targets ≥ 40×40px on mobile.
- Every interactive element is keyboard reachable, has a visible focus style, and an accessible
  name. Icon-only buttons need `aria-label`. Images need `alt` (empty for decorative).
- Loading, empty and error states exist and say something useful.
- No new console errors or warnings on the screens you touched.

## Performance

- The main bundle is ~2.8 MB already. Do not import heavy libraries into the entry chunk; lazy-load
  routes or modals with `lazy()` when adding something large.
- Check `vite build` output size before and after. Call out growth over 50 KB.

## How to check

- Signed-out screens: `node .cursor/skills/amixof-prod-check/scripts/prod-check.mjs --base <url>`
  takes screenshots at all four combinations and checks scroll, console errors and branding.
- Locally: `pnpm --filter client exec vite build && pnpm --filter client exec vite preview --host`
  then run the same script with `--base http://localhost:4173`.
- Look at the screenshots. A script passing is not the same as the page looking right.
